{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-66209-r4510607","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Marinated Green Olives","sourcePageId":66209,"sourceRevision":"4510607","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-17T13:05:24Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Marinated%20Green%20Olives&oldid=4510607","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:24.620Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Appetizer recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using fennel seed","Category:Recipes using ground cumin","Category:Recipes using lemon","Category:Recipes using olive","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Spanish recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"4dbd7b3e186dcb7fb0998a2561b7e2d89420b33b705c87eb4559347f4836368b","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Olive recipes\n| Yield = 1 pound (450 g)\n| Time = Prep: about 10 minutes</br>Marinating: 3–7 days\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nGreen olives [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinated]] in herbs and garlic are very common in Spanish restaurants. They are commonly served free when you order a drink, and are often served with toasted, salted nuts.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (16 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]]/450 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) unpitted large green Spanish [[Cookbook:Olive|olives]]\n*7 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n*½ medium [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] dried [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n*1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Fennel|fennel]] seeds\n*½ teaspoon dried [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n*½ teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] seeds\n*½ teaspoon dried [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]]\n*½ teaspoon Spanish [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n*½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Lightly crush the olives with a mallet, or make slight slits on each olive with a knife, to ensure that the marinade permeates them.  \n# Place the olives in a sealable glass jar and add the remaining ingredients.  \n# Fill the jar with water and shake well.  \n# Marinate at room temperature for several days to a week.\n# Serve the olives with toasted [[Cookbook:Almond|almonds]] and fresh [[Cookbook:Bread|bread]].\n\n[[Category:Recipes using olive|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Spanish recipes]]\n[[Category:Appetizer recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fennel seed]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Marinated Green Olives","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups (16 oz/450 g) unpitted large green Spanish olives","sourceText":"2 cups (16 oz/450 g) unpitted large green Spanish olives","amountText":"2 cups (16 oz/450 g) unpitted large green Spanish olives","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"7 cloves garlic, peeled and minced","sourceText":"7 cloves garlic, peeled and minced","amountText":"7 cloves garlic, peeled and minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3"